TI  - A Novel Multi-Modal Neural Framework for Deep Learning-Based Psychometric Assessment: Enhancing Cognitive and Emotional Intelligence with Attention-Guided Fusion
AU  - P. R. S
AU  - S. Minish T N
AU  - A. P. V
AU  - P. K. N
AU  - S. G
T2  - 2025 2nd International Conference on New Frontiers in Communication, Automation, Management and Security (ICCAMS)
AB  - In recent years, psychometric assessment has evolved beyond traditional questionnaire-based evaluations, thanks to advances in deep learning and multi-modal data processing. Conventional methods often fail to capture the dynamic, complex nature of human cognition and emotional intelligence, which are critical for real-world decision-making and interpersonal interactions. To bridge this gap, we propose "A Novel Multi-Modal Neural Framework for Deep Learning-Based Psychometric Assessment", focusing on the integration of diverse data sources such as text, facial expressions, voice tonality, and physiological signals — to deliver a more holistic and accurate understanding of an individual's mental and emotional capabilities. Our approach employs an attention-guided fusion mechanism, which dynamically prioritizes the most relevant features across different modalities. By doing so, the model not only improves the precision of cognitive and emotional assessments but also provides interpretable insights into the factors influencing the results. This fusion of deep learning with psychometrics represents a significant step forward in the development of intelligent, adaptive assessment tools that are more aligned with the complexities of human behaviour. This framework opens up new possibilities for personalized learning, mental health monitoring, talent acquisition, and human-centric AI systems, offering transformative benefits across education, healthcare, and corporate sectors.
