TI  - Intelligent Assessment Algorithm of Mental Health Status based on Multimodal Data Fusion
AU  - L. Zuo
AU  - M. Che
AU  - J. Chen
T2  - 2025 3rd International Conference on Data Science and Information System (ICDSIS)
AB  - This paper aims to solve the problem of how to accurately evaluate mental health status. It uses multimodal data fusion technology to fuse text and image data for research. First, text data covering the description of mental state and image data showing facial expressions are collected, and the text data is cleaned and pre-processed by word segmentation, and the image data is enhanced. Then, the word vector model and long short-term memory network are used to process the text, and the convolutional neural network and faster regional convolutional neural network are used to process the image. The evaluation model is constructed through early fusion, late fusion, and fusion based on the attention mechanism. After experimental evaluation, the performance of each fusion model in terms of accuracy, F1 score and other indicators is different. The fusion method based on the attention mechanism has obvious advantages in capturing the key information of text and image, with an accuracy of 95.6% and an F1 score of 96.0%, providing a more effective way for the intelligent evaluation of mental health status.
