AU  - Y. Zhang
AU  - T. Fang
T2  - 2025 5th International Conference on Machine Learning and Intelligent Systems Engineering (MLISE)
AB  - This study propose a multimodal approach for detecting social anxiety disorder (SAD) using microblog data. Visual features are extracted via CNNs, while textual cues are analyzed using the deepseek-R1 language model guided by DSM-5-based prompts. A late fusion strategy combines these features for final classification. By integrating visual and textual modalities, our method overcomes limitations of unimodal approaches. Experimental results show improved diagnostic accuracy, highlighting the effectiveness of multimodal learning for SAD detection.
