TI  - TI-Fusion: A Multimodal Anxiety Disorder Detection Method
AU  - M. Shadid
AU  - M. S. Afnan
AU  - M. J. A. Patwary
T2  - 2023 6th International Conference on Electrical Information and Communication Technology (EICT)
AB  - Anxiety disorder significantly impacts individuals’ well-being and daily functioning, emphasizing the need for early detection and accurate diagnosis. However, relying solely on unimodal data for machine learning approaches can produce misleading or inaccurate results. To address this issue, this paper presents a non-intrusive late multimodal fusion technique that integrates text and image data, resulting in a highly accurate unified output. Six different machine learning algorithms are utilized, ideally suited for analyzing the textual data within the particular dataset (DASS-21). These algorithms excel at extracting meaningful patterns, classifying and making accurate predictions based on textual data. Simultaneously, image data (KDEF, CK+) is processed using a Convolutional-Neural-Network (CNN) equipped with real Gabor-filter. CNN effectively captures texture, edges, and complex visual patterns, enabling precise image analysis and recognition tasks. A late multimodal fusion algorithm (Text-Image Fusion) is employed to combine the outputs from both modalities. This approach achieved a final accuracy of 97.62%.
